{"Conditional passkeys/webAuthn form setup is now gated on the user being non-null, which may change when/where conditional UI is available (e.g., on the initial username+password screen before user identification). Need to confirm this is intended for all flows (first-login, login-hint, remember-me, and error challenges) and that conditional UI still appears when expected.": 0.4427143931388855, "The new hook method to control whether authenticators are shown is overridden without an explicit override annotation, which can hide signature mismatches and makes refactors riskier. Should add an explicit override marker to ensure the intended polymorphic behavior.": 0.2523869276046753, "The new tests use broad exception catching (Exception) around element lookup to assert absence of WebAuthn UI, which can mask unrelated failures (timing, stale elements, driver issues). Should narrow the exception type (e.g., NoSuchElementException) or use a helper/assertion that explicitly checks element absence.": 0.7772674560546875}